Requirements: 10   with obligations: 10

[task-01] Add a third way of building a mutation edit: drive a headless coding agent
    over a copy of the project and ask it for what the one-call builder is asked for —
    the smallest edit that makes one named defect true. Claude Code is the first agent
    it can drive. The agent is chosen by a setting, and supporting another agent, such
    as Codex, means adding that agent's adapter without changing the builder.
    -> headless-coding-agent-mutation-edit  [functional/explicit]
       Add a third way of building a mutation edit by driving a headless coding agent
       over a copy of the project and asking it for the smallest edit that makes one
       named defect true.
    -> claude-code-first-agent  [functional/explicit]
       Claude Code is the first agent it can drive.
    -> agent-chosen-by-setting  [functional/explicit]
       The agent is selected by a setting.
    -> adapter-added-without-builder-change  [compatibility/explicit]
       Supporting another agent, such as Codex, is accomplished by adding that agent's
       adapter without changing the builder.

[task-02] The agent builder is a fallback, never the first attempt. It is asked about a
    defect only when every candidate the existing builder produced for that defect was
    set aside, and only when it has been configured; with nothing configured a review
    behaves exactly as it does today.
    -> existing-builder-candidates-exhausted  [functional/explicit]
       The agent builder is asked about a defect only after every candidate the existing
       builder produced for that defect has been set aside.
    -> configured-agent-builder-gating  [functional/explicit]
       The agent builder is used only when it has been configured.
    -> preserve-current-review-behavior-when-unconfigured  [compatibility/explicit]
       Preserve the current review behavior when nothing is configured.

[task-03] Its edit gets no privileged path. What the agent changed in the copy is
    reduced to one span replacement in one file and then goes through the same checks as
    any other candidate: the text checks, the test run against the usable tests, the
    breadth refusal and the broken-edit check. If what it changed is not a single
    contiguous edit inside a region the defect names, the candidate is set aside rather
    than repaired. An unverified agent edit carries no more weight in the review than
    any other unverified edit.
    -> no-privileged-path  [invariant/explicit]
       The edit receives no privileged path; it is treated like any other unverified
       edit and goes through the same checks as any other candidate.
    -> single-span-replacement-in-one-file  [invariant/explicit]
       The agent's change in the copy is reduced to one span replacement in one file.
    -> same-checks-as-other-candidates  [functional/explicit]
       The candidate goes through the same checks as any other candidate: the text
       checks, the test run against the usable tests, the breadth refusal, and the
       broken-edit check.
    -> single-contiguous-edit-inside-named-region  [invariant/explicit]
       The candidate is set aside when the change is not a single contiguous edit inside
       the region the defect names.
    -> unverified-edit-no-privilege  [invariant/explicit]
       An unverified agent edit carries no more weight in the review than any other
       unverified edit.

[task-04] The agent cannot read the project's tests. The copy it works in has the test
    files removed, so the restriction holds whatever the agent is told or decides to do.
    -> cannot-read-project-tests  [human_review/explicit]
       The agent cannot read the project's tests.
    -> test-files-removed  [docs_config/explicit]
       The copy it works in has the test files removed.
    -> restriction-holds-regardless-of-agent-action  [invariant/explicit]
       The restriction holds whatever the agent is told or decides to do.

[task-05] What a run records is the agent's diff, not its transcript. A replayed review
    reuses the recorded diff without starting the agent, and two replays of the same
    input are byte-identical. A run that exceeds its time limit, fails, or changes
    nothing yields no usable answer.
    -> record-agent-diff  [functional/explicit]
       Record the agent's diff, not its transcript.
    -> replayed-review-reuses-recorded-diff  [functional/explicit]
       A replayed review reuses the recorded diff without starting the agent.
    -> byte-identical-replays  [invariant/explicit]
       Two replays of the same input are byte-identical.
    -> no-usable-answer-on-timeout-failure-or-no-change  [functional/explicit]
       A run that exceeds its time limit, fails, or changes nothing yields no usable
       answer.

[task-06] Each defect sent to the agent records what the attempt cost in dollars and how
    long it took on the wall clock, next to the same figures for the one-call builder's
    attempts at that defect, so the two can be compared.
    -> defect-attempt-cost-and-duration-recorded  [functional/explicit]
       Each defect sent to the agent records the attempt cost in dollars and the wall-
       clock duration.
    -> one-call-builder-attempt-figures  [functional/explicit]
       Record the one-call builder's attempt cost in dollars and wall-clock duration
       next to the same figures for the defect so the two sets of figures can be
       compared.

[exclusion-01] A Codex adapter. Only Claude Code is driven in this change.
    -> codex-adapter-only-claude-code-driven  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change is limited to adding a Codex adapter, and Claude Code is the only
       agent driven in this change.

[exclusion-02] Making the agent builder the first attempt or the default.
